@@ -41,6 +41,24 @@ RelayBoard is a small job-control application with:
 
 The implementation should remain small enough that a reviewer can inspect the whole system.
 
+## Archiving Jobs
+
+`POST /api/jobs/{id}/archive` hides a Job from `/api/jobs` and the Jobs
+dashboard. `POST /api/jobs/{id}/restore` reveals it again. Both endpoints
+return HTTP 200 with the Job, including its `archived` boolean; repeated
+requests are idempotent. Unknown Job IDs return HTTP 404.
+
+Archived Jobs reject new manual and scheduled Runs with HTTP 409. Runs
+already in progress continue with the existing retry and alert behavior,
+and Run history, Attempts and Alerts are retained. Archiving and restoring
+preserve the enabled/disabled state. Enable/disable updates while archived
+return HTTP 409; restore the Job before changing that state.
+
+Archive state is persisted in SQLite. Existing databases receive an
+`archived` column with all existing Jobs initially unarchived.
+
+Verify with `python -m unittest discover -s tests -v`.
+
 ## Treatment isolation
 
 Treatment agents receive the fixture workspace and scenario prompt.
